WEBVTT

00:11.011 --> 00:13.139
[rock music playing]

00:43.043 --> 00:44.503
Seriously? Math really said that?

00:44.587 --> 00:45.796
CHAPTER 50:
A CLASSIC, NOT A CLICHÉ

00:45.880 --> 00:46.964
I'm telling you he did.

00:47.757 --> 00:48.591
[chuckles]

00:48.674 --> 00:51.552
-So, how about this one?
-Uh, no.

00:52.386 --> 00:53.387
This one?

00:55.055 --> 00:56.724
[sighs deeply]

00:56.807 --> 00:59.435
The problem is we don't know
what kind of style he prefers.

00:59.518 --> 01:01.270
Feminine or sexy?

01:02.980 --> 01:05.232
I think he likes both feminine and sexy.

01:05.941 --> 01:07.485
He seems quite greedy, you know?

01:08.235 --> 01:09.528
[gasps] Oh, hold on a sec.

01:10.029 --> 01:12.323
VIDEO CHATTING
EUI-JU, GO-YA

01:12.406 --> 01:13.574
Huh?

01:13.657 --> 01:15.326
[whimsical music playing]

01:15.409 --> 01:16.410
Ta-da.

01:17.953 --> 01:19.121
Seriously?

01:19.955 --> 01:20.956
You don't think

01:21.582 --> 01:22.750
it's a good choice?

01:23.250 --> 01:26.128
For a first date, it doesn't work?
[clicks tongue]

01:26.212 --> 01:27.213
[Woo-su] Eui-ju.

01:27.963 --> 01:28.964
Yes?

01:29.757 --> 01:30.841
What's your plan Saturday?

01:30.925 --> 01:31.926
[sighs]

01:32.635 --> 01:35.054
What on Earth could he want to talk about…

01:35.137 --> 01:37.973
[gasps] …just the two of us this weekend?

01:38.682 --> 01:40.309
[chuckles]

01:40.392 --> 01:41.852
Ah, I don't know.

01:42.394 --> 01:43.813
[breathes deeply]

01:43.896 --> 01:45.940
So what should I wear? [groans]

01:49.235 --> 01:52.071
[groans] Why is it only Thursday?

01:55.449 --> 01:58.369
[groans] Why is it only Friday?

02:00.871 --> 02:02.832
It's almost Saturday already.

02:03.707 --> 02:06.710
But why is time passing so slowly?

02:12.591 --> 02:13.676
[groans, sniffles]

02:17.680 --> 02:18.639
[exclaims]

02:19.223 --> 02:20.474
[bell rings]

02:21.350 --> 02:22.476
[server] Welcome.

02:22.560 --> 02:23.561
EPISODE 16

02:23.644 --> 02:26.313
-Did you have a reservation?
-Uh, yes. Probably. Yes.

02:26.397 --> 02:27.523
May I have the name for it?

02:27.606 --> 02:28.649
It's Ga Woo-su.

02:31.360 --> 02:32.653
Uh… I don't have it.

02:34.697 --> 02:35.823
Yeo Eui-ju?

02:35.906 --> 02:36.907
Yeo Eui-ju…

02:38.868 --> 02:39.952
Not that either.

02:41.370 --> 02:42.538
Anyway, there'll be two of us.

02:42.621 --> 02:44.915
-[chuckles] Sure. Please come this way.
-Yes. Thank you.

02:51.797 --> 02:53.799
[server]
Ma'am, let me get some water for you.

02:53.883 --> 02:54.884
Thank you.

02:56.594 --> 02:58.721
All right.
Please let me know if you need anything.

02:58.804 --> 02:59.805
Okay.

03:05.352 --> 03:07.563
What do I do? I'm so nervous.

03:08.147 --> 03:11.025
[Go-ya] Don't show it though.
He won't find you attractive.

03:11.692 --> 03:14.111
Order cream pasta. You know why, right?

03:14.194 --> 03:15.988
[Eui-ju] That's too much of a cliché.

03:16.530 --> 03:19.158
[Go-ya] Mm-mmm.
It's a classic, not a cliché.

03:19.241 --> 03:20.367
Trust me on this.

03:20.451 --> 03:23.203
[gentle romantic music playing]

03:31.337 --> 03:32.713
[server] Welcome.

03:39.178 --> 03:42.681
[tense music playing]

03:43.933 --> 03:44.934
[Eui-ju sighs]

03:54.902 --> 03:58.030
I guess Mr. Ga invited us to help us
patch things up.

03:59.281 --> 04:00.282
I guess so.

04:05.746 --> 04:07.206
-[door opens]
-[bell rings]

04:07.289 --> 04:08.332
[server] Welcome.

04:08.916 --> 04:09.917
You guys are early.

04:10.000 --> 04:11.126
-Did you have a reservation?
-Yes…

04:11.210 --> 04:12.670
…under "after-school" for 12 people.

04:12.753 --> 04:16.674
Uh… We have one under "Actors' School",
not "after-school" though.

04:16.757 --> 04:18.467
It's "after-school". After.

04:19.051 --> 04:19.885
[server chuckles]

04:19.969 --> 04:21.845
-Oh, it's still for 12 people, right?
-Yes.

04:21.929 --> 04:24.014
All right. Please have a seat there.

04:24.098 --> 04:25.224
Why are you guys there?

04:27.434 --> 04:28.435
[sighs]

04:30.062 --> 04:32.982
-[students chattering]
-Oh, my gosh. This place is so nice.

04:33.691 --> 04:34.942
[student 1] Looks so good.

04:37.611 --> 04:39.488
-Thank you.
-Ah, I can't wait.

04:39.571 --> 04:41.740
I appreciate your hard work.

04:41.824 --> 04:42.825
Why don't we have a toast?

04:42.908 --> 04:44.535
-[student 2] Sounds great.
-[student 3] Sure.

04:44.618 --> 04:45.619
Good job.

04:45.703 --> 04:46.870
-Thank you!
-Thank you!

04:46.954 --> 04:47.997
[student 4] Thank you!

04:48.080 --> 04:50.749
Hey, why are you guys
all dressed up today?

04:50.833 --> 04:52.668
I know, you guys look so pretty today.

04:52.751 --> 04:55.045
Be… Because it's Saturday. [chuckles]

04:56.380 --> 04:57.631
This is awesome.

05:01.844 --> 05:02.845
[sighs]

05:02.928 --> 05:03.929
[phone vibrates]

05:04.013 --> 05:05.889
[student 5] Mr. Ga, this is to die for.

05:05.973 --> 05:08.600
[Go-ya] How's the date going?
Send me some pictures.

05:09.268 --> 05:11.979
-Mr. Ga, can I have some of that too?
-Sure, go ahead.

05:12.062 --> 05:13.731
-[student 5] Huh? Me too.
-Yes. [chuckles]

05:13.814 --> 05:14.815
[student 4] I want some too.

05:14.898 --> 05:18.610
Okay, should we take a pic
for the memories?

05:18.694 --> 05:20.738
-[chuckles]
-Sounds good. Let's do it.

05:20.821 --> 05:22.656
We need a picture together.
For sure. For sure.

05:22.740 --> 05:23.991
[chuckles]

05:26.535 --> 05:27.911
[with mouth full]
Wait, you're blocking me.

05:27.995 --> 05:30.581
One, two, three.

05:30.664 --> 05:32.499
WITH MR. GA
AFTER-SCHOOL MATH FINISHED

05:32.583 --> 05:33.792
[students cheering]

05:39.256 --> 05:40.758
[alarm beeping]

05:43.927 --> 05:44.928
[grunts]

05:46.055 --> 05:47.056
[beeping stops]

05:48.474 --> 05:49.558
[sighs]

05:51.226 --> 05:52.269
[yawns]

05:54.730 --> 05:56.023
[sighs]

05:57.608 --> 05:59.651
[somber music playing]

06:24.259 --> 06:25.260
[breathes shakily]

06:26.970 --> 06:27.971
Dong-ju.

06:30.349 --> 06:31.350
Dong-ju.

06:32.351 --> 06:33.352
[door opens]

06:33.435 --> 06:34.436
[Dong-ju] What is it?

06:37.439 --> 06:38.440
I can't see.

06:38.941 --> 06:39.942
[Dong-ju] What?

06:42.069 --> 06:43.320
Take me to the hospital.

06:43.821 --> 06:45.280
Okay, hold on.

06:46.782 --> 06:48.742
Hey, Gi-jeon. Gi-jeon. Wake up.

06:48.826 --> 06:50.953
-[Gi-jeon] What? What is it?
-[Dong-ju] Woo-su has a problem.

06:58.085 --> 06:59.920
[machine beeping]

07:06.969 --> 07:08.303
I can't see.

07:15.602 --> 07:18.856
[doctor] So your right eye had
a total corneal transplant before?

07:19.940 --> 07:20.941
Yes.

07:21.024 --> 07:25.696
What we can do for you now is
a deep anterior lamellar keratoplasty.

07:26.238 --> 07:29.741
It replaces part of the cornea
except for the inner endothelial layer.

07:32.119 --> 07:33.245
[Dong-ju sighs]

07:34.496 --> 07:36.248
He had the surgery ten years ago.

07:36.748 --> 07:37.749
He was fine.

07:37.833 --> 07:39.710
-No side effects afterward.
-Exactly.

07:41.545 --> 07:43.172
We all thought he was okay.

07:43.255 --> 07:44.381
So why…

07:44.464 --> 07:45.549
[sighs]

07:46.425 --> 07:47.676
[crying]

07:48.552 --> 07:49.553
Hey.

07:50.387 --> 07:51.388
Are you

07:52.806 --> 07:53.849
crying?

07:54.850 --> 07:56.852
I feel so bad for that bastard.

07:56.935 --> 08:00.814
[sobs] I knew when he played the smart-ass
and read all those damn papers.

08:00.898 --> 08:02.649
I knew this would happen, but…

08:02.733 --> 08:05.152
He didn't listen
and became a teacher, damn it.

08:05.235 --> 08:07.154
I've been worried sick every single day.

08:07.237 --> 08:09.823
In case he'd end up like this
and give up on his studies.

08:09.907 --> 08:10.824
[sobs]

08:10.908 --> 08:12.951
-He's gonna be all right.
-[sniffles]

08:13.660 --> 08:15.621
Hey, what happened to all that trash talk?

08:16.205 --> 08:17.206
Hey, come on.

08:17.289 --> 08:19.625
You know how much he cares for Woo-su.

08:20.417 --> 08:21.752
TREATMENT ROOM 1

08:22.961 --> 08:24.838
[gasping]

08:28.175 --> 08:30.552
-Please register at the reception.
-Oh, okay.

08:32.137 --> 08:33.138
Are you all right?

08:33.805 --> 08:34.806
Yeah.

08:35.474 --> 08:36.850
So, what's the problem?

08:36.934 --> 08:38.435
[Da-ju gasps] Hey, you're just an idiot!

08:38.518 --> 08:40.270
You think you're so smart

08:40.354 --> 08:42.481
but can't even take care
of your goddamn eyes.

08:42.564 --> 08:44.399
Why can't you do that one simple thing

08:44.483 --> 08:46.193
when all you do
is scold people for nothing,

08:46.276 --> 08:47.736
you arrogant prick?

08:48.820 --> 08:50.822
-Calm down, okay? Calm down.
-[breathes shakily]

08:50.906 --> 08:52.074
I'm getting surgery.

08:53.992 --> 08:56.036
Will that make your eyes better?

08:56.620 --> 08:57.871
[somber music playing]

08:58.372 --> 08:59.915
[doctor] Well, honestly speaking,

08:59.998 --> 09:03.627
there's a 50% chance
that your vision will recover to

09:04.753 --> 09:06.004
its pre-surgery state.

09:08.006 --> 09:12.052
Your cornea is exceptionally thin,
and the situation is quite complicated.

09:13.387 --> 09:16.139
Just don't exert yourself
and get plenty of rest

09:16.223 --> 09:17.975
until the surgery, okay?

09:18.850 --> 09:20.060
I'm going to get admitted,

09:20.727 --> 09:23.397
and they'll see
if my condition is suitable for surgery.

09:23.480 --> 09:24.481
[sniffles]

09:24.564 --> 09:26.400
Don't make a fuss and go home.

09:26.483 --> 09:28.193
Let's get you admitted first.

09:37.286 --> 09:39.955
-[chattering]
-[door opens]

09:41.915 --> 09:43.792
-Hi.
-[students] Hello.

09:43.875 --> 09:45.627
-Hello.
-He's here.

09:45.711 --> 09:47.087
[Dong-ju] Hello, everyone.

09:47.170 --> 09:50.090
[sighs] Your homeroom teacher won't be
coming to school for the time being,

09:50.173 --> 09:52.092
due to his eye problem.

09:52.175 --> 09:53.760
So I'm here on his behalf.

09:54.594 --> 09:56.638
I'll be taking attendance.

09:57.514 --> 09:58.974
Mr. Yoon, Mr. Yoon.

09:59.558 --> 10:00.767
How bad is his condition?

10:00.851 --> 10:02.269
What exactly is wrong with him?

10:03.103 --> 10:04.187
Uh…

10:04.271 --> 10:08.025
[sighs] I remember you said overdoing
himself would put his other eye at risk.

10:08.108 --> 10:09.443
What did you mean by that?

10:09.526 --> 10:11.403
If he's away for the time being,

10:11.486 --> 10:12.821
is he hospitalized?

10:12.904 --> 10:14.656
How long will he stay at the hospital?

10:16.116 --> 10:18.577
Eui-ju, don't you have a class to go to?

10:18.660 --> 10:21.997
[breathes shakily]
Which hospital is he staying at, huh?

10:22.080 --> 10:25.292
Just tell me that.
You can tell me that much, can't you?

10:25.375 --> 10:26.376
[sighs]

10:28.920 --> 10:30.589
[doctor] Your cornea is a bit thin,

10:30.672 --> 10:33.884
but there shouldn't be any major problems
in proceeding with the surgery.

10:33.967 --> 10:37.512
It will definitely help sharpen your focus
and improve you vision in general.

10:40.223 --> 10:42.934
[somber music playing]

10:46.396 --> 10:48.648
-[sighs]
-[chuckles] Come on.

10:49.733 --> 10:50.734
Are you scared?

10:50.817 --> 10:52.319
[scoffs] No, I'm not.

10:52.402 --> 10:55.447
-[Gi-jeon chuckles]
-You were really in pain before,

10:55.530 --> 10:57.115
but you look all right now.

10:57.199 --> 10:58.283
[inhales deeply]

10:58.367 --> 11:02.162
Can't you have them do something
to make your double eyelids thicker?

11:02.245 --> 11:03.955
[chuckles]

11:04.456 --> 11:06.792
You don't do
personality transplants here, do you?

11:07.542 --> 11:08.585
[sighs]

11:11.254 --> 11:12.672
[sighs]

11:12.756 --> 11:14.424
Come on, man. Don't be a wuss.

11:15.717 --> 11:16.718
Good luck.

11:17.344 --> 11:18.512
See you later, four eyes.

11:18.595 --> 11:19.596
-[chuckles]
-Wait…

11:19.679 --> 11:20.889
You don't have glasses.

11:20.972 --> 11:22.099
So, "geek" will do.

11:22.182 --> 11:23.183
[chuckles]

11:23.892 --> 11:25.143
You're feeling okay, right?

11:26.978 --> 11:27.979
Good luck, huh.

11:28.814 --> 11:29.981
It's time to go now.

11:30.649 --> 11:31.650
Okay.

11:31.733 --> 11:32.901
See you.

11:32.984 --> 11:34.528
Don't cry, okay?

11:36.196 --> 11:37.739
-[Da-ju exhales sharply]
-Goodness.

11:37.823 --> 11:38.824
Yeah.

11:42.160 --> 11:43.161
[exhales sharply]

11:49.876 --> 11:51.294
[dramatic music playing]

11:52.170 --> 11:53.839
-Huh? What? Eui-ju?
-Hey!

11:53.922 --> 11:55.048
Hey, Eui-ju.

11:55.132 --> 11:56.842
Hey, Eui-ju. Where are you going?

11:56.925 --> 11:58.802
-[Go-ya] Where?
-[Dan-ji] Did you see her face?

11:58.885 --> 12:01.888
[Dong-ju] He asked me to keep it a secret
until his surgery is over.

12:01.972 --> 12:04.850
He probably didn't tell anyone
in case they worried.

12:04.933 --> 12:06.977
He's at Hana University Medical Center.

12:12.107 --> 12:13.108
[doctor sighs]

12:13.608 --> 12:18.155
Fortunately, the surgery
went smoother than we previously expected.

12:18.238 --> 12:20.282
Are you feeling uncomfortable in any way?

12:20.365 --> 12:21.658
-No, I'm all right.
-[chuckles]

12:23.368 --> 12:25.704
May I ask when I'll be able
to start reading again?

12:26.288 --> 12:27.873
Uh, give it about a week.

12:27.956 --> 12:30.625
It'll still be uncomfortable,
but you should be able to read.

12:32.169 --> 12:36.381
Full visual comfort though,
that could take three or four weeks.

12:36.882 --> 12:38.091
I see. Thank you.

12:38.175 --> 12:40.844
[chuckles]
You just need to focus on recovering.

12:40.927 --> 12:42.137
[chuckles]

12:43.847 --> 12:45.390
[door opens]

12:46.558 --> 12:47.767
[sighs]

12:48.351 --> 12:49.603
[rapid footsteps approach]

12:53.648 --> 12:55.358
[gasps]

12:59.029 --> 13:00.030
[breathes shakily]

13:03.200 --> 13:05.327
Eui-ju, two demerit points
for ditching school.

13:05.410 --> 13:07.204
[breathing heavily]

13:09.915 --> 13:11.166
[breathes shakily]

13:13.168 --> 13:14.169
[whimpers]

13:15.587 --> 13:16.588
Mr. Ga.

13:17.255 --> 13:18.548
Are you okay, though?

13:22.260 --> 13:24.763
[breathes shakily]
Just tell me if you're okay.

13:27.015 --> 13:29.518
About your ridiculous
absolute-value question…

13:32.020 --> 13:33.480
My answer is…

13:38.735 --> 13:40.362
the promise from ten years ago.

13:43.365 --> 13:45.283
[child crying]

13:45.367 --> 13:47.744
[poignant music playing]

13:51.122 --> 13:53.333
Hey, are you in a lot of pain?

13:56.378 --> 13:57.379
YEO EUI-JU

13:57.462 --> 13:59.005
[young Eui-ju] It's my mom.

13:59.089 --> 14:03.385
She said she won't let me
watch Pichi Pichi Pichi

14:03.468 --> 14:06.221
if I get the questions wrong again.

14:06.304 --> 14:07.764
[crying continues]

14:07.847 --> 14:08.974
[crying stops]

14:09.057 --> 14:10.433
Open your hands like this.

14:11.851 --> 14:14.646
Twelve means
all ten of your fingers plus two more.

14:14.729 --> 14:17.232
One, two, three, four, five…

14:18.567 --> 14:20.193
-It's seven.
-That's right.

14:20.735 --> 14:22.946
So now whenever you do subtraction,

14:23.029 --> 14:26.157
try doing it from the two-digit number,
not the one-digit number.

14:26.241 --> 14:30.996
Does that mean that the ten-digit friend
is lending a hand to its one-digit friend?

14:31.079 --> 14:32.455
That's really nice.

14:33.164 --> 14:35.083
[young Woo-su] Right.
Let's try another question.

14:35.166 --> 14:38.128
[young Eui-ju]
Look, maybe I'm a genius now.

14:38.211 --> 14:40.380
Math is super easy.

14:40.463 --> 14:41.464
[chuckles]

14:41.548 --> 14:45.885
Now I'll get 100 on my math work,
and I'll show you the next time we meet.

14:46.469 --> 14:47.596
I promise.

14:49.723 --> 14:50.932
[giggles]

14:51.016 --> 14:52.017
[chuckles]

14:52.767 --> 14:53.977
Hmm.

14:58.690 --> 15:01.192
We met again ten years after that day.

15:01.276 --> 15:02.360
Yeo Eui-ju?

15:03.695 --> 15:05.322
-Yeo Eui-ju!
-Over here.

15:06.698 --> 15:08.074
Four points.

15:08.658 --> 15:09.784
[Woo-su] A four in math?

15:11.536 --> 15:14.122
[chuckles] You just hate math, huh?

15:14.706 --> 15:18.335
You can't imagine the struggle
watching you try to keep that promise.

15:20.420 --> 15:22.297
Wow… [gasps]

15:22.380 --> 15:25.425
Those destined to meet
always do after all.

15:26.176 --> 15:27.886
We're meant to be.

15:27.969 --> 15:29.095
What?

15:30.513 --> 15:31.514
Uh, nothing.

15:31.598 --> 15:33.808
[chuckles] It's nothing.

15:33.892 --> 15:35.644
I remember now.

15:35.727 --> 15:38.855
You're that boy.
The handsome guy who was good at math.

15:38.938 --> 15:41.191
Whoa. [chuckles]

15:41.274 --> 15:42.359
You remembered?

15:42.859 --> 15:44.027
You have no excuse now.

15:44.110 --> 15:45.111
Hold on.

15:45.654 --> 15:47.280
[gasps] This means,

15:47.364 --> 15:50.617
I was eight when I met you
for the first time

15:51.660 --> 15:54.537
and that's earlier than
when Deul-i met you, is that right?

15:54.621 --> 15:55.914
What?

15:55.997 --> 15:57.999
[chuckles] Yes. I win.

15:58.083 --> 16:00.835
[scoffs] Are you serious?

16:01.544 --> 16:02.545
[chuckles]

16:02.629 --> 16:03.505
[scoffs]

16:03.588 --> 16:04.839
Anyway,

16:04.923 --> 16:06.841
is she not coming to visit?

16:06.925 --> 16:08.426
She's got no reason to.

16:08.510 --> 16:10.887
But isn't she… Isn't she your girlfriend?

16:11.471 --> 16:13.348
Not at all. We're just friends.

16:13.431 --> 16:14.641
Oh, come on.

16:14.724 --> 16:17.268
You have a different look on your face
when you're with her.

16:17.352 --> 16:19.354
You smile a lot. A sweet smile, you know?

16:19.437 --> 16:20.772
Something like this.

16:20.855 --> 16:23.525
Don't you smile when you're with a friend?

16:24.025 --> 16:25.193
Is that it?

16:26.069 --> 16:27.070
[clears throat]

16:27.153 --> 16:28.655
Then maybe… [inhales sharply]

16:28.738 --> 16:30.448
I can get my hopes up a little.

16:31.032 --> 16:31.908
What?

16:33.868 --> 16:34.869
Nothing.

16:35.829 --> 16:37.122
I wish you a quick recovery.

16:37.706 --> 16:38.707
[chuckles]

16:39.207 --> 16:40.542
Go home. I'm tired.

16:41.209 --> 16:42.752
-[grunts]
-Yep.

16:44.212 --> 16:45.922
-[sighs]
-[Eui-ju] Goodbye.

16:46.005 --> 16:47.674
Eui-ju, help me with this
before you leave.

16:48.508 --> 16:49.759
Sure! [giggles]

16:50.635 --> 16:51.761
I'm home.

16:52.345 --> 16:53.680
-Hey, Mom.
-[with mouth full] Welcome home.

16:53.763 --> 16:55.640
-Mom, Mom, Mom, Mom, Mom.
-Hmm. What is it?

16:55.724 --> 16:58.893
Remember, remember when you took me
to that hospital in Seoul,

16:58.977 --> 17:00.311
what's that hospital called?

17:01.187 --> 17:03.398
What?
What are you talking about right now?

17:03.481 --> 17:04.691
This is so random.

17:04.774 --> 17:06.985
You know,
you took me to that hospital in Seoul,

17:07.068 --> 17:08.445
back when I was in first grade.

17:08.528 --> 17:12.490
What? Why would you see a doctor
when your mom's a pharmacist?

17:12.574 --> 17:15.326
You've never been sick enough
to go to a hospital.

17:16.703 --> 17:18.371
That's not true. I have.

17:18.455 --> 17:20.540
[indistinct voices on television]

17:21.541 --> 17:22.542
I haven't?

17:23.168 --> 17:24.169
You haven't.

17:27.464 --> 17:29.799
Dad, I haven't?

17:32.093 --> 17:33.094
Huh?

17:33.720 --> 17:34.721
What the…

17:35.764 --> 17:36.765
When was it then?

17:39.142 --> 17:40.393
W-w-was it someone else?

17:40.477 --> 17:42.604
[mysterious music playing]

17:43.813 --> 17:44.939
[interviewer] Mr. Ga,

17:45.023 --> 17:47.567
you were well known for
being a math prodigy

17:47.650 --> 17:48.943
when you were just a young boy.

17:49.027 --> 17:50.403
CHAPTER 51:
THE NONSENSE ABSOLUT VALUE

17:50.487 --> 17:52.864
Could you tell me
what inspired you to become a teacher?

17:55.784 --> 17:57.619
Just before my second Olympiad,

17:58.203 --> 17:59.704
I withdrew from the competition.

18:00.580 --> 18:02.874
The official reason
was deteriorating eyesight,

18:03.458 --> 18:06.127
but the real reason was something else.

18:06.211 --> 18:07.921
During training camp,
I met this one other guy.

18:08.004 --> 18:09.380
GA WOO-SU
MATH TEACHER, MURIM GIRLS' HIGH

18:09.464 --> 18:11.216
He was always late because he overslept.

18:11.299 --> 18:14.469
He'd get caught reading comics
during problem-solving sessions.

18:14.552 --> 18:17.847
And yet, he breezed through
every problem I couldn't solve.

18:17.931 --> 18:19.140
-[Eui-ju chuckles]
-Bang.

18:19.224 --> 18:21.017
[Woo-su]
It was the first time I felt humbled.

18:21.100 --> 18:22.644
[chuckles]

18:22.727 --> 18:26.231
I could tell he had outstanding intuition
and that he genuinely loved math.

18:26.815 --> 18:29.150
I knew I'd keep meeting people like that
through life,

18:30.318 --> 18:32.445
and I just didn't have
the confidence to keep going.

18:32.529 --> 18:34.489
I thought, "what should I do now?"

18:35.365 --> 18:36.825
I got my eye surgery,

18:36.908 --> 18:38.868
after dropping out of the Olympiad,

18:39.452 --> 18:42.413
and, at the hospital, I met a little girl.

18:45.041 --> 18:46.876
In that child's bright eyes,

18:46.960 --> 18:48.962
and the way she jumped up and down
with excitement,

18:50.004 --> 18:53.007
I was reminded of the moment
I first fell in love with math.

18:53.967 --> 18:55.844
And for someone who
had only ever been a student,

18:56.594 --> 18:58.429
it was the very first time

18:59.180 --> 19:01.683
that I felt true joy
in teaching someone else.

19:01.766 --> 19:03.101
[sighs]

19:03.184 --> 19:04.185
[interviewer] I see.

19:04.269 --> 19:06.479
So, I'm guessing that student
followed in your footsteps,

19:06.563 --> 19:09.190
competed in the Olympiad,
and obviously are really good at math.

19:11.860 --> 19:12.861
Well…

19:13.695 --> 19:15.738
life rarely goes the way you want it to.

19:19.325 --> 19:21.619
-[chuckles]
-Has she lost it?

19:22.996 --> 19:24.163
Now one last thing,

19:24.873 --> 19:28.334
can you tell us
what does math mean to you, Mr. Ga?

19:30.503 --> 19:31.504
[inhales sharply]

19:31.588 --> 19:33.339
TEACHERS' OFFICE

19:33.423 --> 19:35.383
[poignant music playing]

19:35.466 --> 19:36.968
[Woo-su] Math is…

19:40.597 --> 19:42.557
-Hello, Mr. Ga.
-Hello.

19:43.224 --> 19:44.225
[Woo-su] Math is…

19:45.810 --> 19:46.811
a process

19:47.437 --> 19:50.231
of discovering my own limits
at every single moment.

19:54.777 --> 19:56.779
[student 6] Oh, yeah. I can't wait.

19:56.863 --> 19:58.531
[student 7]
I wonder when he's gonna come in.

19:58.615 --> 20:00.783
-Oh, hello.
-Hello.

20:08.499 --> 20:10.168
[mouthing] I got 55 points.

20:11.586 --> 20:12.587
[sighs]

20:19.844 --> 20:22.263
Great job on making it through
another boring school year.

20:22.347 --> 20:24.807
Yes, that's right.
We went through so much!

20:24.891 --> 20:26.351
-Good job, everyone!
-Yeah, we did it!

20:26.434 --> 20:27.810
-Good job, girls!
-We went through so much…

20:27.894 --> 20:29.270
-[laughing]
-…but we did it!

20:31.689 --> 20:33.066
And now you're gonna be seniors.

20:33.149 --> 20:34.651
[students groan]

20:34.734 --> 20:37.153
If you just spend your vacation
having fun,

20:38.196 --> 20:39.447
you'll regret it in March.

20:40.156 --> 20:42.241
I'm not telling you
to focus only on studying.

20:42.325 --> 20:43.576
Evaluate yourself.

20:43.660 --> 20:45.536
Know what you like and dislike.

20:46.120 --> 20:48.873
Learn what you're capable of
and what you want to achieve.

20:55.588 --> 20:56.589
Keep moving forward.

21:01.552 --> 21:04.389
I want you to have faith in
whatever path you choose, and walk on it.

21:04.472 --> 21:06.474
No matter what anyone else says.

21:11.229 --> 21:12.355
Each one of you

21:13.356 --> 21:14.357
is…

21:16.693 --> 21:18.736
a star that shines differently.

21:19.404 --> 21:20.905
[groaning]

21:20.989 --> 21:22.281
Oh, Mr. Ga.

21:22.365 --> 21:23.866
[students clamoring]

21:23.950 --> 21:25.326
It's sweet.

21:27.954 --> 21:30.331
I can't take it. He's so sweet.

21:30.415 --> 21:32.041
[student 8] That was so sweet.

21:35.586 --> 21:38.256
[student 9] Aw, Mr. Ga. I love him.

21:38.339 --> 21:39.382
Dismissed.

21:40.425 --> 21:43.720
-Aw, thank you.
-Thank you.

21:43.803 --> 21:45.930
[students chattering, giggling]

21:46.014 --> 21:47.015
[student 10] Bye, Mr. Ga!

21:47.098 --> 21:48.933
[cheering]

21:49.017 --> 21:50.893
["Sweet & Sour" playing]

21:50.977 --> 21:52.020
CHAPTER 52:
I'M GLAD WE MET

21:52.103 --> 21:54.397
-[Eui-ju] What do you think?
-[Dan-ji] I really like it.

21:54.480 --> 21:57.692
"You and I are the closest at heart.

21:58.484 --> 22:00.403
A star that's distant for a moment,

22:00.486 --> 22:02.739
but close for a long time."

22:03.781 --> 22:05.074
-What do you say?
-Oh. [chuckles]

22:05.158 --> 22:06.534
Eui-ju and Go-ya, huh?

22:07.201 --> 22:09.162
-This is pretty nice.
-Not bad at all, you know.

22:09.245 --> 22:10.288
[Dan-ji] I give you that!

22:10.371 --> 22:11.831
-[laughs] Nice job.
-[Jenny] I love it.

22:11.914 --> 22:13.124
I really do.

22:13.207 --> 22:15.084
-[Yeong-jae] You're the best.
-We did do a good job.

22:15.168 --> 22:17.587
[Dan-ji] "Close for a long time."
This is totally us. Don't you think?

22:17.670 --> 22:19.255
-[Yeong-jae] It's so like us!
-[Dan-ji] Oh, Eui-ju.

22:20.590 --> 22:23.134
Oh. I'll visit you for sure, okay?

22:23.217 --> 22:24.218
It better be soon.

22:24.302 --> 22:25.720
Okay. I'll make it real soon.

22:27.680 --> 22:29.265
-[sighs] Jenny.
-[chuckles]

22:29.348 --> 22:31.017
Don't forget about us.

22:32.435 --> 22:34.854
And don't ever dare to leave
our group chat, okay?

22:35.438 --> 22:37.940
I'll annoy you with emoji bombs
all the time.

22:38.024 --> 22:39.192
Please do.

22:39.275 --> 22:40.902
[both chuckling]

22:41.819 --> 22:42.987
All right. Bye, Jenny.

22:43.071 --> 22:44.489
[groaning]

22:45.073 --> 22:47.909
Well, make sure you get
a boyfriend by the time you come back.

22:47.992 --> 22:49.994
[all laughing]

22:50.078 --> 22:51.079
I will.

22:51.162 --> 22:53.414
Anyway, what's taking Eui-ju so long, huh?

22:53.498 --> 22:54.916
There she comes.

22:55.541 --> 22:57.418
-Run, guys!
-[Dan-ji] Eui-ju, hurry!

22:57.502 --> 22:59.504
-[Yeong-jae] What took you so long?
-You're so late!

22:59.587 --> 23:00.838
Come on, Ji-a… [panting]

23:00.922 --> 23:03.841
Ji-a wanted to say goodbye to Jenny,
and I waited until she was done working.

23:03.925 --> 23:05.218
Hey, when did I say that?

23:05.301 --> 23:06.594
Yes, you did. [laughs]

23:06.677 --> 23:10.348
Ji-a. Ji-a. Mmm.

23:10.431 --> 23:12.266
I can't get used to her hyper personality.

23:12.350 --> 23:13.351
I get it though.

23:13.434 --> 23:15.394
You guys are like a cat and a dog.

23:15.478 --> 23:16.979
-Meow! Woof! Woof!
-[chuckling]

23:17.063 --> 23:18.356
So true.

23:18.439 --> 23:20.983
I'm sorry that
I didn't look after you better.

23:21.067 --> 23:22.485
Take care of yourself out there.

23:22.568 --> 23:23.778
And eat this on your way.

23:25.154 --> 23:27.782
[groaning] Oh, my deskmate.

23:27.865 --> 23:29.784
-[all laughing]
-[Eui-ju] Geez.

23:30.409 --> 23:32.036
-Oh, don't cry.
-Thank you.

23:32.120 --> 23:34.288
Jenny, this is for you too.

23:34.372 --> 23:36.499
Take care and don't ever forget us, okay?

23:37.083 --> 23:37.917
Mmm.

23:39.377 --> 23:40.586
Ta-da!

23:40.670 --> 23:42.171
A STAR FAR AWAY

23:42.255 --> 23:43.422
[all] Whoa! [laughing]

23:44.215 --> 23:46.551
-[laughing]
-[gasps]

23:46.634 --> 23:48.094
[Dan-ji] No, it should be mine.

23:48.177 --> 23:49.178
Eui-ju.

23:49.262 --> 23:52.098
[groans] Aw…

23:52.181 --> 23:54.767
Aw, I'm going to miss you.

23:54.851 --> 23:56.102
-Mmm.
-Me too.

23:56.185 --> 23:57.103
Thank you.

24:00.022 --> 24:01.357
[kisses]

24:01.440 --> 24:02.441
[all laughing]

24:02.525 --> 24:04.443
-Bye!
-Bye, Jenny! We love you!

24:04.527 --> 24:05.862
[Jenny chuckling]

24:05.945 --> 24:08.406
Guys, I'm right here!

24:09.574 --> 24:11.325
[chuckles] I'm here.

24:12.285 --> 24:14.579
[chuckles] I love you, girls!

24:15.955 --> 24:17.039
Be safe!

24:17.123 --> 24:18.875
-Bye, bye, bye, bye!
-Bye, Jenny!

24:23.087 --> 24:24.463
[chuckles] See you soon!

24:25.464 --> 24:27.133
Bye! Love you!

24:29.093 --> 24:30.261
[sighs]

24:31.596 --> 24:33.681
I'm really happy I got to meet you all.

24:34.849 --> 24:35.850
[gasps]

24:37.685 --> 24:41.647
Thank you for making
every day full of fun and laughter.

24:42.315 --> 24:45.443
Every memory I have here in Korea
is with you girls,

24:45.526 --> 24:46.652
and…

24:47.570 --> 24:50.031
and I loved every single moment.

24:50.948 --> 24:53.951
I might be leaving,
but our friendship is forever.

24:54.702 --> 24:56.245
We'll meet again.

24:57.246 --> 24:59.665
Thank you for welcoming me warmly

24:59.749 --> 25:02.835
and making good memories with me.

25:02.919 --> 25:04.212
See you again.

25:04.295 --> 25:05.379
Let me take your picture.

25:05.463 --> 25:06.923
-Good idea.
-Do it, do it, do it.

25:07.006 --> 25:08.507
-Stand here.
-[Dan-ji] Beautiful Korea.

25:09.634 --> 25:10.760
[shutter clicks]

25:10.843 --> 25:12.762
-Tteokbokki. I like tteokbokki.
-Do you like tteokbokki?

25:12.845 --> 25:15.056
-Yeah.
-You do? It's so good.

25:15.139 --> 25:17.099
If you like spicy food,
you should try jjampong.

25:17.183 --> 25:19.101
What do you say to fried chicken or pizza?

25:19.185 --> 25:20.478
[laughing]

25:20.561 --> 25:22.480
[Eui-ju]
I was able to finish writing the novel,

25:22.563 --> 25:25.900
thanks to the support of my readers,
who desperately wanted me to resume.

25:27.526 --> 25:31.697
Later, the novel was launched
and reached over a million downloads.

25:32.365 --> 25:34.367
It's so exciting. [gasps]

25:34.450 --> 25:37.286
I became a top-tier writer at last.

25:37.370 --> 25:39.288
Oh, you want to know how it ended?

25:40.122 --> 25:43.292
WE WERE FRIENDS, FINAL EPISODE

25:51.968 --> 25:53.719
[inhales sharply, sighs]

25:54.595 --> 25:55.846
Okay. Fine.

25:56.347 --> 25:58.766
Now that I know
your heart belongs to Kang Tae-ha,

25:58.849 --> 25:59.809
[scoffs]

25:59.892 --> 26:00.977
I'll stop right now.

26:01.060 --> 26:03.396
-Si-on.
-[sighs]

26:03.479 --> 26:05.231
I told myself I'd never regret this.

26:06.065 --> 26:07.066
Turns out I do.

26:09.568 --> 26:11.279
I always was mean to you, wasn't I?

26:11.362 --> 26:13.614
Thanks for everything, Choi Yoon!

26:13.698 --> 26:15.992
Come on, don't act like
we'll never see each other again.

26:16.075 --> 26:18.286
Today will be the last time.

26:19.078 --> 26:20.121
Is that necessary?

26:20.204 --> 26:22.748
Si-on, you were my world in high school.

26:24.792 --> 26:26.711
I don't want to lose you.

26:28.587 --> 26:29.672
[scoffs]

26:31.007 --> 26:32.591
I know I'm the winner,

26:33.718 --> 26:35.344
but, strangely,
I don't feel pleased at all.

26:35.928 --> 26:37.096
You think this is a game?

26:37.179 --> 26:39.432
What do you win, huh?
A medal or something?

26:41.350 --> 26:42.685
You bastard.

26:42.768 --> 26:43.728
[tense music playing]

26:43.811 --> 26:45.313
[both breathing heavily]

26:47.023 --> 26:48.190
Uh, don't do this.

26:48.941 --> 26:49.942
-Huh?
-[sighs]

26:53.029 --> 26:54.155
I'm leaving.

26:54.739 --> 26:56.532
[gasps] Hey, Si… No, wait.

26:56.615 --> 26:58.200
[Jae-min] Well…

26:58.284 --> 26:59.744
You guys were all here.

27:01.412 --> 27:03.039
I looked everywhere for you.

27:03.122 --> 27:05.958
Sit down. Sit down. Sit. Come.

27:09.253 --> 27:11.672
What's going on? What's with this mood?

27:11.756 --> 27:13.549
Did someone die or something?

27:13.632 --> 27:15.718
[laughing]

27:16.344 --> 27:18.054
I'm not in the mood for jokes now.

27:18.721 --> 27:19.930
You got dumped?

27:20.014 --> 27:22.016
-[sighs] Uh…
-[sighs]

27:22.933 --> 27:24.685
So you're giving up?

27:26.395 --> 27:27.271
No…

27:28.272 --> 27:30.649
I'm not giving up on Yoon!

27:30.733 --> 27:32.151
-Hey, Han Jae-min.
-What? What?

27:32.234 --> 27:33.694
What do you want?

27:33.778 --> 27:34.653
Damn.

27:34.737 --> 27:38.824
Yoon, are you okay with
cutting ties with Si-on?

27:39.325 --> 27:40.618
No, right?

27:40.701 --> 27:42.078
Tae-ha, you too, punk.

27:42.161 --> 27:45.831
Are you sure you can be happy
while Yoon is sad?

27:55.716 --> 27:56.926
Let's all live together!

27:58.886 --> 27:59.929
Huh?

28:00.513 --> 28:02.306
-Together?
-The four of us.

28:03.349 --> 28:04.975
What's the big deal?

28:05.476 --> 28:08.562
You never truly know someone
until you've lived with them.

28:08.646 --> 28:09.647
-[sighs]
-Only then…

28:11.273 --> 28:12.691
you get to know their true colors.

28:13.401 --> 28:14.693
Uh…

28:14.777 --> 28:17.405
-[Jae-min laughs]
-Still, it's unnecessary to live together.

28:17.488 --> 28:20.241
Getting cold feet?
Then chicken out while you can.

28:20.324 --> 28:21.617
Ha! There's no way.

28:21.700 --> 28:24.078
[scoffs] I'm more than ready for it.

28:24.161 --> 28:25.788
[scoffs]

28:25.871 --> 28:27.998
-Still, I don't think this is--
-[shushes]

28:29.667 --> 28:30.584
[shushes]

28:30.668 --> 28:32.002
Don't worry,

28:32.086 --> 28:34.588
my baby deer.

28:34.672 --> 28:36.006
-[chuckles]
-Huh?

28:36.632 --> 28:38.217
It'll be super fun.

28:39.844 --> 28:40.845
As if.

28:41.345 --> 28:43.013
It's going to be a living hell.

28:43.097 --> 28:44.098
[chuckles]

28:46.434 --> 28:47.560
Is this round two?

28:48.394 --> 28:49.395
Oh, please.

28:51.355 --> 28:53.107
All right, let's go!

28:53.190 --> 28:55.526
Here we come. Home, sweet home!

28:55.609 --> 28:57.403
Whoo! Bang, bang!

28:57.486 --> 28:59.071
All right, let's go!

29:09.832 --> 29:14.462
MOST POPULAR WEB NOVEL OF 2026
WE WERE FRIENDS

29:15.463 --> 29:16.505
[Shin] Here you go. [groans]

29:16.589 --> 29:17.673
FINAL CHAPTER:
FIRST SNOW

29:18.257 --> 29:19.341
-Honey…
-[grunts]

29:19.425 --> 29:22.011
…do you remember this?

29:22.094 --> 29:23.762
Oh, man. Yeah.

29:23.846 --> 29:27.308
This is when I went to the ER
for food poisoning. [groans]

29:27.391 --> 29:28.392
The ER?

29:29.435 --> 29:30.436
[Shin] Huh?

29:30.519 --> 29:33.981
Remember that time you fed me
all those raw oysters to boost my stamina,

29:34.064 --> 29:35.816
and I… [groans]

29:35.900 --> 29:38.027
[Ma] Oh, you mean when we went to Seoul?

29:53.250 --> 29:54.293
What's going on?

29:56.170 --> 29:57.630
You're leaving tomorrow, right?

29:57.713 --> 29:59.006
Are you done packing up?

29:59.840 --> 30:02.009
Mmm. Are you saying goodbye?

30:04.595 --> 30:06.597
[Eui-ju] I came to give you this.

30:13.604 --> 30:16.690
I-I hear medical fees are expensive

30:16.774 --> 30:19.235
and it's not easy
getting medicine in the States.

30:19.318 --> 30:20.653
What if you get sick there?

30:22.112 --> 30:24.657
[inhales sharply]
You absolutely cannot get sick.

30:24.740 --> 30:28.536
And make sure you don't get too close
with Deul-i while you're over there.

30:28.619 --> 30:32.414
But don't go getting close
with the American girls either.

30:32.915 --> 30:35.459
Just study
and come straight back, all right?

30:36.126 --> 30:39.129
Oh, and watch out
for pretty American girls…

30:39.213 --> 30:42.258
Oh, and cute guys too.

30:42.341 --> 30:44.260
I guess you never know, right?

30:44.343 --> 30:48.305
And if anyone talks to you,
do not smile at them ever.

30:48.389 --> 30:49.431
Got it?

30:50.349 --> 30:51.350
[chuckles]

30:52.226 --> 30:53.602
Thank you. [chuckles]

30:54.270 --> 30:55.521
[groans]

30:55.604 --> 30:58.023
Oh, you really shouldn't smile like that.

30:58.607 --> 31:00.484
[sighs] This is not good at all.

31:02.736 --> 31:05.114
You're going to study
and do your research in the States

31:05.197 --> 31:06.865
only during vacation, right?

31:07.491 --> 31:09.243
You have to come back, okay?

31:10.119 --> 31:11.453
You don't have to worry.

31:12.371 --> 31:13.831
And good luck with your writing.

31:14.623 --> 31:16.208
What's your next project?

31:17.376 --> 31:18.419
[chuckles]

31:19.086 --> 31:20.296
The title is…

31:26.260 --> 31:28.137
[whispering]

31:29.722 --> 31:31.599
["Why the Night" playing]

31:35.352 --> 31:37.062
-[sighs]
-[chuckles]

31:38.314 --> 31:39.607
Have a safe trip.

31:40.983 --> 31:43.819
Thanks. Stay safe okay.

32:41.877 --> 32:44.338
[exclaiming]

32:44.421 --> 32:46.632
Mr. Ga! Mr. Ga!

32:47.216 --> 32:48.801
Mr. Ga, come back out!

32:49.635 --> 32:51.261
Look, it's snowing!

32:51.345 --> 32:53.555
It's the first snow! [laughs]

32:53.639 --> 32:55.224
The first snow.

32:57.017 --> 32:58.435
[laughs] It's snowing!

32:59.269 --> 33:01.230
Mr. Ga, it's the first snow!

33:07.027 --> 33:08.362
[Woo-su] Is that exciting?

33:11.407 --> 33:12.616
[Eui-ju] Of course!

33:13.409 --> 33:15.285
My first snow!

33:15.953 --> 33:17.371
The first snow!

33:18.038 --> 33:19.790
[laughs] My first snow!

34:03.333 --> 34:05.252
[students clamoring]

34:09.214 --> 34:11.550
["Sweet & Sour" playing]

35:10.901 --> 35:12.986
[students]
♪ Everything is sweet and sour ♪

35:14.655 --> 35:17.032
[in Korean] ♪ This might be the real me ♪

35:18.617 --> 35:20.828
[in English]
♪ Everything is sweet and sour ♪

35:21.411 --> 35:23.789
[in Korean] ♪ Fill it sweetly ♪

35:23.872 --> 35:25.624
[in English] ♪ Sweet and sour ♪

35:25.707 --> 35:27.960
[cheering]

35:28.043 --> 35:29.586
-[song stops]
-[chairs clatter]

35:33.507 --> 35:35.384
[cheering]

35:35.467 --> 35:36.510
[song resumes]

35:52.901 --> 35:56.780
[chanting]

35:56.864 --> 35:59.157
-Jenny!
-Jenny!

35:59.241 --> 36:01.326
[cheering continues]

36:08.542 --> 36:10.961
[all, in Korean]
♪ What's really on your mind ♪

36:11.044 --> 36:12.629
♪ If you feel uneasy ♪

36:12.713 --> 36:14.464
[in English] ♪ You know it's all right ♪

36:14.548 --> 36:17.050
[in Korean]
♪ When you look up to the sky ♪

36:17.134 --> 36:20.220
[in English] ♪ It's sweet and sour ♪

36:20.304 --> 36:22.806
♪ Everything is sweet and sour ♪

36:23.599 --> 36:26.310
[in Korean] ♪ This might be the real me ♪

36:27.769 --> 36:30.105
[in English]
♪ Everything is sweet and sour ♪

36:30.772 --> 36:32.649
[in Korean] ♪ Fill it sweetly ♪

36:32.733 --> 36:35.110
[in English] ♪ Sweet and sour ♪

36:42.784 --> 36:45.495
[cheering]

36:45.579 --> 36:46.830
-Bye!
-Bye!

36:54.379 --> 36:57.132
THE END
